## 🚀 Overview

**Real-time image enhancement on FPGA edge devices** — this project delivers a hardware-accelerated pipeline using Residual Convolutional Neural Networks deployed via Vitis AI.

> Transform degraded images (low-light, noisy, blurry) into high-quality results at **8× faster inference** than CPU, with minimal power consumption.

### Key Capabilities

| Capability | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| ⚡ Real-time FPGA inference | Sub-second processing on edge hardware |
| 🧠 Edge AI deployment | Production-ready for embedded systems |
| 🌙 Low-light enhancement | Recover details from dark scenes |
| 🧹 Noise reduction | Remove sensor/grain noise |
| 🔍 Blur restoration | Sharpen motion/out-of-focus blur |
| 📦 INT8 quantization | 4× memory reduction vs FP32 |

---

## ✨ Key Features

- **Residual CNN Architecture** — Skip connections for stable gradient flow and superior image quality
- **INT8 Quantization-Aware Training (QAT)** — Preserve accuracy while enabling hardware acceleration
- **FPGA DPU Deployment** — Leverage Xilinx Deep Learning Processor Unit
- **End-to-End Vitis AI Workflow** — From PyTorch model to `.xmodel` deployment
- **Docker-Based Reproducibility** — One-command environment setup
- **Comprehensive Benchmarking** — PSNR, SSIM, latency, and throughput metrics
- **Real-Time Inference Pipeline** — Ready for streaming video applications

---

## 🧠 System Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[📸 Degraded Dataset] --> B[🧠 Residual CNN Training]
    B --> C[📉 Quantization-Aware Training]
    C --> D[🔢 INT8 Optimization]
    D --> E[🛠️ Vitis AI Compilation]
    E --> F[📦 XModel Generation]
    F --> G[⚡ DPU Deployment]
    G --> H[🖥️ FPGA Inference]
    H --> I[✨ Enhanced Output]
    
    style A fill:#f9f,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style I fill:#9f9,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style G fill:#ff9,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
